==English==
{{was wotd|2020|June|12}}

===Etymology===
{{unknown|en|Origin unknown}}; perhaps from {{der|en|el|μαλακός|t=soft; compliant, meek; gentle, mellow, mild, mild-mannered}} or {{m|el|μαλακία|t=masturbation; (''figuratively'') idiocy, stupidity; bullshit, nonsense}}. The word was popularized by the Irish-American [[cartoonist]] [[w:Tad Dorgan|Thomas Aloysius (“Tad”) Dorgan]] (1877–1929), who started using it in cartoons on March 9, 1922.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=112775|date=June 2000}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|author=Mark Memmot|title=What’s All this Malarkey about Malarkey?|url=https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2012/10/12/162791655/whats-all-this-malarkey-about-malarkey|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190606155406/https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2012/10/12/162791655/whats-all-this-malarkey-about-malarkey|archivedate=6 June 2019|work={{w|NPR}}|date=12 October 2012}}.</ref>

